# Developer kernel: debugfs back on. Never a shipping config.
#
#   KERNEL_CONFIG=debug build/build.sh kernel   ->  build/out/h713-kernel-debug.fit
#   KERNEL_CONFIG=netboot,debug ...             ->  the usual bench kernel
#
# The release defconfig has CONFIG_DEBUG_FS off since 12.09.2026 (Marco: "kein
# Debug im Release"). That closes /sys/kernel/debug/cpu_comm/call -- the prompt
# that sends any RPC by name straight to the display firmware -- along with the
# tx_delay_* knobs, the write side of cpu_comm/watch, and the read-only status
# files of hdmirx and cpu_comm. Every measurement in doku/nachtlog/ that quotes
# "cpu_comm/call", "cpu_comm/watch" or "h713-tv ctl rpc" needs this fragment.
#
# Nothing else changes: same drivers, same device tree, same bootargs. The
# elog level of the MIPS firmware is not a kernel setting at all; it is
# ELOG_LEVEL in display_cfg.xml, written by U-Boot only when "h713_disp init"
# is given elog=<0-5>, and raised at run time from Linux through /dev/mem at
# 0x4b48bd9c (doku/63-mips-elog.md). This fragment does not touch it.
CONFIG_DEBUG_FS=y
CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG=y
